{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00151","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00151@rel:R19-11#0d644a1d","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00151","release":"R19-11","content":"If the CSM module reports a recoverable error (example: E_BUSY, QUEUE_FULL) during authentication of an Authentic I - PDU , the SecOC module shall not provide a Secured I - PDU to the lower layer. It shall keep that Authentic I - PDU (if not overwritten by an incoming Authentic I - PDU of the same type) to start the authentication with the next call of the scheduled main function until the number of additional authentication attempts for that Authentic I - PDU has reached its limits.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_SecureOnboardCommunication.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:15+00:00","text_key":"4761b65619d8"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00151@rel:R20-11#a42520d3","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00151","release":"R20-11","content":"If the CSM module reports a recoverable error (example: E_BUSY, QUEUE_FULL) during authentication of an Authentic I - PDU , the SecOC module shall not provide a Secured I - PDU to the lower layer. It shall keep that Authentic I - PDU (if not overwritten by an incoming Authentic I - PDU of the same type) to start the authentication with the next call of the scheduled main function until the number of additional authen tication attempts for that Authentic I - PDU has reached its limits.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_SecureOnboardCommunication.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:34+00:00","cleaning":{"rule":"spec-text-clean@1","raw_sha256":"a42520d33943bd6c04096d98484e1f8873cde08e3b59b094d1401fe72616199b","removed":["Specification of Secure Onboard Communication AUTOSAR CP R20 - 11 55 of 179 Document ID 654 : AUTOSAR_SWS_SecureOnboardCommunication"]},"text_key":"4761b65619d8"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/re